                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "It's not a game for everyone.\nI can't evaluate whether the game is scary (both games and movies don't scare me - something about a screen being between me and the scary world strips the fear away :/).\n\nIt's a walking simulator, and some of the places in it are just a little bit too far apart for a protagonist who doesn't walk or run that fast (though he jumps really high :D) — but the Lovecraftian atmosphere is there, and atmosphere is what I came here for.\n\nI really liked the fact that this game did not use Unreal/Unity. It has its distinct style that I really like. The UI is a little crude (but does its job), the sound is fine although the protagonist's footsteps sound really weird, which was confusing at the beginning. The story is simple but serviceable, most of the puzzles (if you can even call them puzzles) are quite simple and you always know what to do, so they don't slow you down.\n\nThere is this entity that follows you sometimes, and in the beginning it gave a feeling of being hunted, but later it became quite irritating. I don't know if I missed something, but the behaviour of the entity is very inconsistent, and it's not always clear what the right path/thing to do is when the entity tries to get to you. Sometimes sneaking works, sometimes running works, sometimes it spawns right in front of you and there is nothing you can do. There were moments when I knew I had chosen the wrong path and just waited for the entity to grab me, as there was no other option. Checkpoints are located quite regularly, so it was not a problem. At worst I had to retry/replay like 30 seconds a few times, but still I think this mechanic was not enriching the experience. Also, the entity model is really, really ugly when seen up close and doesn't fit the rest of the game :D\n\nI think the game would benefit from being a little shorter and from the entity mechanic being designed a little bit better, but overall, it was a really enjoyable experience for me.",
